   "blocked": 0,
   "final_text": "Samira Qureshi's hire (E1025, case-1959b9ef, starting 2026-11-02) is fully handled. It turned out to be a rehire, so I reused her old account rather than creating a new one. The feed has been quiet for about 50 minutes and nothing I started is still pending.\n\n**Why it was treated as a rehire:** Two former workers had the same name: E1023, a Software Engineer, and E1024, a Sales Rep. The new record had no government ID token or rehire link to tell them apart, so I asked HR to confirm before creating anything. HR confirmed she is the same person as E1024.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Identity:**\n  - Our policy is to reuse a rehire's old account, so I re-pointed her old account (acct-2be88b46, samira.qureshi2@example.com) to the new worker record as an Employee.\n  - I gave her a new mailbox. Her old mailbox stays as a shared mailbox, untouched.\n  - I added only the standard groups for a Software Engineer: All-Staff, VPN-Users and Eng-Git. The separation-of-duties check found no conflicts. Policy says not to restore old access, and the old account had none anyway.\n  - I enabled the account because her start date is today.\n- **Work email in Workday:** I wrote samira.qureshi2@example.com back to her Workday record. The update completed and her record now shows it. The one new event in the feed (seq 2) was just the confirmation of that update.\n- **Equipment:** I ordered the engineering laptop bundle (ticket tkt-92c9357d). Delivery is tracked in ITSM.\n- **Finance:** I created her finance profile with cost center CC-1000 and her manager, Avery Carter (E1001), as expense approver.\n- **Workday onboarding tasks:** \"Create accounts and email\" and \"Provision equipment\" are both marked Complete.\n\nHer new record still has no government ID token on file, so HR may want to add one; that would let future rehires be matched to her automatically."
  }
